Zram-private LZ4 block codecs
============================

upstream/ contains unmodified lib/lz4.c, lib/lz4.h, lib/lz4hc.c and
lib/lz4hc.h from https://github.com/lz4/lz4, tag v1.11.1, commit
aa4647fad575d01a874aaaadcdbe8e6a40e072f5. Preserve their BSD license notices.

Only the zram LZ4 and LZ4HC backends include these sources. Entry points
have internal linkage, so they do not replace the kernel's public LZ4
symbols or change filesystem and boot-decompressor workspaces or behavior.
The freestanding headers and lz4_deps.h adapt ISO C dependencies and
linkage without changing the imported files. Codec workspaces are
allocated when a zram context is created, not during page compression.
LZ4HC uses the extended workspace introduced in LZ4 v1.11.0, allowing
levels 10 through 12 without allocating or using a large kernel stack.

The integration follows the vendoring approach proposed by Michal
Wilczynski for lib/lz4 (v2, November 6, 2026):
https://lore.kernel.org/all/20261106-lz4-vendor-upstream-v2-0-ee04c3f0d7dc@samsung.com/
The dictionary template optimization follows android-mainline commit
f0f6f7871430 (zram: optimize LZ4 dictionary compression performance).
Neither source is represented as a merged v1.11.1 lib/lz4 update.

To update, copy the four release files verbatim, then check both backends
with and without dictionaries, mixed page contents, legacy decoder
compatibility, malformed blocks, and constrained output buffers.
